# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WHAT NEVER GOES UP TO VERCEL in a deploy made from the machine.
#
# Git deploys already respect .gitignore, but `vercel deploy` from the CLI
# packages the FOLDER. Without this, the client's originals
# (public/multimedia/, 681 MB) would be uploaded and end up published at a
# public URL, along with the internal material. Same criterion as the
# _interno/ block in .gitignore: if it's the client's or it's working
# material, it doesn't get published.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
/_interno/
/public/multimedia/
/public/fonts/_drop/
/src/content/_source/
/design-audit/
/docs/
/.playwright-mcp/
.env*
!.env.example
